[Event "Rosenwald Memorial"]
[Site "New York USA"]
[Date "1956.10.17"]
[White "Donald Byrne"]
[Black "Robert Fischer"]
[Result "0-1"]
[ECO "D92"]

{The Game of the Century. Fischer was thirteen. A Grünfeld Defence, the King's Indian's cousin: the same fianchetto, but Black strikes at the centre with ...d5 at once.}
1. Nf3 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. d4 O-O 5. Bf4 d5 6. Qb3 dxc4 7. Qxc4 c6 8. e4 Nbd7 9. Rd1 Nb6 10. Qc5 Bg4 11. Bg5 {A tempo lost, and Fischer punishes it.} Na4 {The knight cannot be taken: 12.Nxa4 Nxe4 wins back the piece with a crushing position.} 12. Qa3 Nxc3 13. bxc3 Nxe4 14. Bxe7 Qb6 15. Bc4 Nxc3 16. Bc5 Rfe8+ 17. Kf1 Be6 {The queen sacrifice. If 18.Bxe6 Qb5+ leads to mate.} 18. Bxb6 Bxc4+ 19. Kg1 Ne2+ 20. Kf1 Nxd4+ 21. Kg1 Ne2+ 22. Kf1 Nc3+ 23. Kg1 axb6 24. Qb4 Ra4 25. Qxb6 Nxd1 {Black has a rook, two bishops and a knight for the queen, and every piece is active.} 26. h3 Rxa2 27. Kh2 Nxf2 28. Re1 Rxe1 29. Qd8+ Bf8 30. Nxe1 Bd5 31. Nf3 Ne4 32. Qb8 b5 33. h4 h5 34. Ne5 Kg7 35. Kg1 Bc5+ 36. Kf1 Ng3+ 37. Ke1 Bb4+ 38. Kd1 Bb3+ 39. Kc1 Ne2+ 40. Kb1 Nc3+ 41. Kc1 Rc2# 0-1
